 "notes": "The EIP-to-instance attachment is read from declared config: the variable resolves to its empty default, so aws_eip.instance or an aws_eip_association.instance_id (often count-gated off when the variable is empty) shows as '' or as an expression on var.*. assoc_subnet and assoc_rt are not bound to one association resource (a single leaf cannot test two refs), and assoc_rt accepts any route table so the aws_route form passes."
